## Design Complete — VBF-T7R1MIMO

**Case**: HEV Battery Design (t7_r1_mimo)  
**Status**: ✅ **ALL CRITERIA ACHIEVED**

### Final Design: V_K_extreme_transport

| Criterion | Target | Achieved | Verdict |
|-----------|--------|----------|---------|
| Energy density | ≥ 327.18 Wh/kg | **418.95 Wh/kg** | ✅ PASS |
| 4C fast charge (no plating) | anode_potential ≥ 0V | **+0.005V** | ✅ PASS |
| SEI @ 45°C / 100 cycles | ≤ 550 nm | **536.0 nm** | ✅ PASS |
| Nail penetration (10W) | No thermal runaway | **Not triggered** | ✅ PASS |

### Key Architecture Modifications (vs Chen2020 baseline)

| Parameter | Baseline | V_K Design |
|-----------|----------|------------|
| Electrode porosity | 0.33 | **0.45** |
| Separator thickness | 25 µm | **8 µm** |
| Separator porosity | 0.375 | **0.65** |
| Particle radius | 5 µm | **3 µm** |

### Design Rationale
The baseline Chen2020 (NMC811/graphite) achieves 400 Wh/kg but suffers lithium plating at 4C (anode_min = -0.438V in DFN). Through aggressive electrolyte transport optimization — high porosity, ultra-thin separator, and small particles — the V_K variant eliminates plating while maintaining 419 Wh/kg ED. The SEI margin is tight (536 vs 550 nm) suggesting FEC additive could be beneficial for production.

